 {"status": "complete", "id": "AUG-169", "title": "A symlinked DIRECTORY resolving outside the corpus root is silently ignored: no refusal, no skipped count, blocks vanish", "detail": {"fingerprint": "b6ebf398c989ca975d8bf30b076b799d866e6f689bf32ea78109d3e587161df1", "evidence": [{"run_id": "afc16739", "ts": "2026-11-14T13:54:41.333933+00:00"}]}, "priority": "P3", "source": null, "reasoning": "Measured 2026-11-13 while grading AUG-148 at 58f5af4 (tier-2 derived criterion, verdict dir 4bd93bbe). Corpus /tmp/a148d/corpus holds real.xml plus sub -> /tmp/a148d/outside where outside/secret.xml carries a sentinel requirement. 'auger spec validate' printed 'spec: 1 document(s), 1 block(s), 0 reference(s) ok' rc 0 and 'spec list' rc 0 named only real.xml: the out-of-root document is neither read (no leak) nor refused nor counted. The file-level rule is enforced (symlink-outside-root, auger.py:8023) and a dangling link is refused as unreadable-document, so the directory shape is the one hole: Path.rglob does not descend symlinked directories and nothing notices. Consequence: a corpus author who links a directory silently loses every block inside it, and AC1 of AUG-148 ('refused with a typed error, or skipped with an explicit count') is only half met.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: pytest tests/test_xml_specs.py -q -k symlinked_directory prints 1 passed — a new test whose corpus holds a symlinked directory resolving outside the root, asserting either a typed refusal or an explicit skipped count that names the link and its target.\nPASS: pytest tests/test_xml_specs.py -q -k symlink prints at least 3 passed — the two shipped file-level pins plus the new directory pin.\nPASS: grep -c tests/test_xml_specs.py tests/gate.sh prints at least 2 — the gate pytest arm still names the file, so the new pin is enforced rather than merely written.\nPASS: no host-file content reaches stdout or stderr — the new test writes a sentinel body into the outside directory and asserts it appears in neither stream nor in the refusal detail.", "complexity": 2, "created_at": "2026-11-13T13:51:40.644396+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-14T13:54:41.333933+00:00", "foreman_note": "Dispatched 2026-11-14 driver tick from origin/main ee6e7bf into /home/kara/worktrees/auger-AUG-169 (wt/AUG-169). Verified at base: _spec_discover_documents iterates root.rglob(\"*.xml\"), which does NOT descend symlinked directories, so an out-of-root symlinked directory is neither read, refused nor counted; shipped pins -k symlink = 2 passed; gate pytest arm names tests/test_xml_specs.py at tests/gate.sh:206. Existing file-level rule (symlink-outside-root at auger.py:8023) and dangling-link rule (unreadable-document) are the precedents to extend. Worker must keep the A2 sweep agreeing and add the new pin in tests/test_xml_specs.py.\n\nClosed on judged PASS afc16739 (.gitreins/history/2026-11-14/afc16739/verdict.json; task_id=AUG-169, commit=09ed733, pass_class=judged). tier1 lint/secrets/tests PASS = bash tests/gate.sh GATE PASS, 729 passed / 2 skipped in 840.16s, LIVE ARMS ran 2 / skipped 0. tier2 9/9 items PASS (5 authored + 4 derived), 0 ungraded, merge_recommendation=no_concerns_found. Implementation 6b806ac merged to main, lifecycle 09ed733 graded; exact-head CI run 43597431860 success. Driver re-measured all four row ACs independently first: 1 passed / 3 passed / grep 2 / out-of-root directory link refused rc 2 symlink-outside-root by BOTH verbs with sentinel count 0 in both streams; A2 sweep 7/7 AGREE. Residual observation (not a defect): an IN-root directory symlink duplicating an already-walked file yields a typed duplicate-id refusal rather than dedupe.", "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": "6b806accea435caad6350fdf46278b591248eba4", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/auger-AUG-169", "branch": "wt/AUG-169", "evidence_run_id": "afc16739"}
 {"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-170", "title": "A missing git binary reaches the user as a raw FileNotFoundError traceback, not a typed spec refusal", "detail": {"fingerprint": "ccc29f894ebdb4394411a5a970c19207032a5ae63dd4727f7f28453c068f391d"}, "priority": "P4", "source": null, "reasoning": "Found by the AUG-123 tier-2 judge as an uncovered failure path; same class as AUG-145 (raw FileNotFoundError where a typed spec error belongs). Obligation resolution shells out to git, and _git_toplevel does not check for the binary.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "When git is not on PATH, obligation resolution shells out and dies with a raw traceback instead of a typed refusal, so the CLI reports a Python crash rather than a spec diagnostic.\n\nMeasured 2026-11-13 at HEAD 830e1cf (venv interpreter, git removed from PATH): `env -i PATH=/home/kara/auger/.venv/bin HOME=/home/kara .venv/bin/python auger.py spec check tests/fixtures/xml/verification` exits **rc 1** with a two-frame traceback ending `FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'git'` raised from `_git_toplevel` (auger.py:13102, `subprocess.run`). The same class as AUG-145 (raw FileNotFoundError where a typed spec error belongs). Found by the AUG-123 judge as an uncovered failure path.\n\nAcceptance criteria (command-shaped; the first is the pre-fix falsifier):\n- PRE-FIX FALSIFIER: `cd /home/kara/auger && env -i PATH=/home/kara/auger/.venv/bin HOME=/home/kara .venv/bin/python auger.py spec check tests/fixtures/xml/verification` currently exits 1 and prints `FileNotFoundError`; after the fix it exits **2** with a typed `spec error (<code>)` line naming the missing git and prints **zero** traceback frames ('Traceback (most recent call last)' count 0).\n- PROOF: the same invocation with a PATH that lacks git returns a code that appears in the verb's documented error vocabulary (grep the chosen code in `auger.py` returns >= 1 and in `docs/VERBS.md` >= 1), so the refusal is not an ad-hoc string.\n- PROOF: both verbs agree under the missing-git environment — `spec validate` and `spec check` on `tests/fixtures/xml/verification` return the SAME rc and the same code.\n- PROOF: with git present, behaviour is unchanged: `.venv/bin/python auger.py spec validate tests/fixtures/xml/verification` exits 0 and `-m pytest tests/test_verification_graph.py tests/test_spec_repository_root.py -q` reports 15 passed.\n- PROOF: a regression test pins it and the gate runs it: the new test node exists in a file named in `tests/gate.sh`'s pytest arm (`grep -c <test-file> tests/gate.sh` >= 1).", "complexity": 2, "created_at": "2026-11-13T20:47:39.918285+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-13T20:47:39.918285+00:00", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": ["xml", "cli", "error-typing"], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null}
