 {"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-181", "title": "Recall registration is not idempotent: every corpus key is stored twice in the auger namespace and duplicate rows consume the retrieval window", "detail": {"metadata": {}, "fingerprint": "9b4bb6bad3c16b264524267988a533bf662bcd4ac1af22e4b350dec236723329"}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": "Measured 2026-11-17 while closing AUG-178 AC4: register was run twice on 2026-11-16 (the second a retry after a 500 on CHD-NORMATIVE-MANIFEST-PREAMBLE-S000-P01) and a memory write APPENDS, so every /auger/AUG176-*/<BLOCK-ID> key resolves to 2 rows. The battery's 'top-5' was therefore a top-2..4 distinct-block measurement (8/12 and 5/12) until the battery itself de-duplicated (11/12 and 9/12 on the same tree). DuckBrain has no DELETE route for a memory row, so the duplication is permanent per prefix and every future register run doubles it again.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "NON-IDEMPOTENT REGISTRATION: `scripts/recall_battery.py register` appends a new memory row every time it runs, and DuckBrain exposes no DELETE route for a memory row, so the `auger` namespace now stores EVERY `/auger/AUG176-*/<BLOCK-ID>` key at least TWICE (measured 2026-11-17: 2 rows for every sampled key). Because the retrieval surface returns one row per stored row, duplicate rows consume the candidate window: the recall battery's \"top-5\" was really \"top-2..4 distinct blocks\" until the battery itself was fixed to de-duplicate (AUG-176/AUG-178). Ranking quality therefore depends on how many times the corpus was registered, which is not something the corpus should encode.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS: any future `register` run (a re-chunk, a corpus refresh, a repaired manifest) doubles the namespace again and dilutes every query's window further; there is no cleanup path through the API, so the damage is permanent per prefix.\n\nAC1 DUPLICATE CENSUS BY READ-BACK: a new `python3 scripts/recall_battery.py census` (or an equivalent documented command) prints, per project, `keys`, `rows`, and `duplicate_keys`, sampled over the whole prefix; expect the numbers to be derived from `GET /api/memories?namespace=auger&prefix=<key>&limit=100` counts and not from a registration log. PROOF: the command's own output committed under evidence/AUG-176/. FAILIF: a count with no read-back command, or a census that samples fewer than 20 keys per project.\n\nAC2 IDEMPOTENT REGISTER: running `register` twice in a row on an already-registered, unchanged corpus writes ZERO new rows the second time — expect the second run to print `rows_written=0` (with `skipped_existing` naming how many keys were already present), and a read-back of any key to still show exactly ONE row for keys registered after the fix. FAILIF: a second run that writes rows, or a post-fix key with more than one row.\n\nAC3 NO LOSS IN THE FIX: every block id of the three corpora still resolves after the change — expect `spec validate` rc 0 on all three corpora, and the recall battery re-run to report per-project hit rates that are NOT lower than the 2026-11-17 baseline (code-factory 11/12, auger-docs 9/12, coding-hermes-director 7/12, total 27/36). PROOF: the three numbers in the committed report. FAILIF: a missing block, or a hit rate below baseline with no cause named.\n\nAC4 HONEST DECISION RECORDED: the row records which path was taken, and the choice is one of (a) register into a FRESH prefix (e.g. `/auger/AUG176b/<BLOCK-ID>`) and point the battery at it, or (b) a substrate-side action that removes duplicate rows, which is duckbrain-owned and must be routed (AUG-180) rather than faked with an allowlist. Expect the row's note to name the prefix the battery reads and the reason the other path was not taken. FAILIF: a fix that rewrites the substrate content, or a battery that quietly tolerates duplicates.\n\nCONTEXT: measured while closing AUG-178 AC4 / AUG-176 AC3 (evidence/AUG-176/06-recall-battery.md, red-proof evidence/AUG-176/07-battery-red-proof.txt). The battery-side de-duplication is already committed; this row is the durable registration-side fix.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-17T06:45:07Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-17T06:45:07Z", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null, "sessions": null, "type": "bug", "initiative": "auger-endstate"}
 {"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-182", "title": "17 complete board rows cite verdict artifacts whose passed=false — the evidence audit reports the class but exits RESULT: OK, so a complete row may stand on a FAILING verdict", "detail": {"fingerprint": "69df33736bdbee3a15283f60ae908d58232f892f0b32f11ae3b8e2497103e195"}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": "Measured by the driver at 1b54668: scripts/audit_board_evidence.py reports bound_failed_verdict=17 (AUG-004, AUG-013, AUG-014, AUG-015, AUG-031, AUG-035, AUG-036, AUG-050, AUG-051, AUG-060, AUG-075, AUG-080, AUG-082, AUG-114, DOC-002, GITREINS-JUDGE, QA-AUGER-6) while RESULT: OK, because ok is defined only as missing==0 and unresolvable==0 (scripts/audit_board_evidence.py:456-460). Spot-checked three: AUG-114 -> 476f5f68 passed=false, DOC-002 -> b9eafc22 passed=false, AUG-004 -> 047fdeed passed=false, each with the same task_id and the row's commit_hash. Goal A12 says a closed row carries RESOLVABLE evidence; a resolvable-but-failing citation is the same false-closeout class that AUG-175/AUG-179 contained for six suffixed-id rows, at larger scale and currently unnamed. Not fixed inline: rewiring a verified row's evidence handle is a verdict-truth change that needs its own judged tree.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "AC1 PROOF: `.venv/bin/python scripts/audit_board_evidence.py --json | jq -r '.bound_failed_verdict | length'` prints 0 — every row named at filing either cites a verdict whose .passed is true or no longer cites a failing run. FAILIF: the count prints above 0.\nAC2 PROOF: for every id printed by the audit, the row's cited verdict reads passed=true OR the row's status is not complete: `.venv/bin/python scripts/audit_board_evidence.py --json | jq -r '.bound_failed_verdict[]'` then per id `jq -r '.passed' .gitreins/history/<date>/<run>/verdict.json` and `jq -r 'select(.id==\"<id>\")|.status'` .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl — each id prints true or a non-complete status, with the reason recorded in its note. FAILIF: any id still complete AND citing passed=false.\nAC3 PROOF: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_board_evidence_audit.py -q` prints all passed, including a NEW test that hands the audit a synthetic complete row citing a passed=false verdict and asserts the row is named as a defect; that new test fails against scripts/audit_board_evidence.py at 1b54668 (red-proof pasted into evidence/AUG-182/). FAILIF: the new test passes unchanged against the pre-fix script, or no new test exists.\nAC4 PROOF: `bash tests/gate.sh` ends GATE PASS with the new test file named in the pytest arm of tests/gate.sh. FAILIF: GATE FAIL, or the test is not in the arm.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-17T12:53:38Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-17T12:53:38Z", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null, "sessions": null, "type": null}
 {"status": "complete", "id": "AUG-183", "title": "CI red on main from 1b54668: tests/test_spec_ingest.py[auger-docs] fails because DOC-021 edited docs/VERBS.md without regenerating the derived corpus block AD-VERBS-SPEC-S018", "detail": {"fingerprint": "d7206ced9a21d6b1be66b33271ff0d3be863f0c12d21e2c17855ff6132b96767", "evidence": [{"run_id": "6db67ef6", "ts": "2026-11-17T15:47:27Z"}]}, "priority": "P1", "source": null, "reasoning": "Measured by the driver: gh run 44081193600 on 1b54668 = failure in 'run the gate (tests/gate.sh)'; the job log names ONE assertion — tests/test_spec_ingest.py:327 AssertionError: auger-docs/AD-VERBS-SPEC-S018 is not a verbatim span of its source. Reproduced locally at cf4c9ad: 1 failed, 2 passed. Cause: DOC-021 (90fb1e1) rewrote the '## spec' section of docs/VERBS.md and the ingest manifest was not re-derived from the new source. Fix shape PRE-VALIDATED by the driver before filing: scripts/ingest_markdown_specs.py auger-docs --out <dir> reproduces deterministically (14 file(s), 139 section(s) -> 139 block(s), 0 skipped) and differs from the tracked corpus in EXACTLY corpora/auger-docs/manifest.json + corpora/auger-docs/VERBS.xml, matching the docs edit. Blast radius: corpus block count stays 139, so the recall battery and any cited counts hold.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "AC1 PROOF: `.venv/bin/python scripts/ingest_markdown_specs.py auger-docs --out corpora/auger-docs` then `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_spec_ingest.py -q` prints all passed (no failed, no error), so every shipped block is a verbatim span of its source again. FAILIF: any failure in tests/test_spec_ingest.py.\nAC2 PROOF: the corpus delta is confined to the derived artifacts — `git diff --stat` names corpora/auger-docs/manifest.json and corpora/auger-docs/VERBS.xml only, and re-running the ingest script into a temp dir diffs clean against the committed corpus. FAILIF: a source doc is reverted to make the test pass, or a corpus file is edited by hand.\nAC3 PROOF: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_spec_ingest.py tests/test_board_evidence_audit.py -q` prints all passed AND `.venv/bin/python scripts/audit_board_evidence.py` ends RESULT: OK. FAILIF: either red.\nAC4 PROOF: exact-head CI on the pushed fix commit is completed/success (read the job log, not the glyph), including the 'run the gate (tests/gate.sh)' step. FAILIF: CI red or unverified on the fix commit.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-17T12:56:19Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-17T15:47:27Z", "foreman_note": "FIXED AND CI-GREEN; awaits a judged verdict. Root cause measured: DOC-021 (90fb1e1) rewrote the '## spec' section of docs/VERBS.md and the derived corpus block AD-VERBS-SPEC-S018 went stale, so tests/test_spec_ingest.py[auger-docs] failed 'is not a verbatim span of its source' (CI 44081193600 on 1b54668; local 1 failed / 2 passed at cf4c9ad). Fix is regeneration, not a hand edit: corpora/auger-docs regenerated with scripts/ingest_markdown_specs.py (14 file(s), 139 section(s) -> 139 block(s), 0 skipped), delta confined to manifest.json + VERBS.xml. Done in the isolated worktree /home/kara/worktrees/auger-AUG-183, rebased onto the board head, ff-merged; commit aab0e5e pushed, parity 0/0. Verified on MERGED main: tests/test_spec_ingest.py 19 passed, scripts/audit_board_evidence.py RESULT: OK, tests/test_board_evidence_audit.py 17 passed. Exact-head CI run 44088060547 on aab0e5e = completed/SUCCESS, read from the job log not the glyph: 'GATE PASS', pytest 584 passed / 215 skipped in 88.40s, LIVE ARMS ran 0 / skipped 2 (AUGER_CI=1, disclosed by the workflow). SECOND FINDING, recorded not fixed: corpora/*/manifest.json embeds ABSOLUTE source_abs paths — my first regeneration ran inside the worktree and baked /home/kara/worktrees/auger-AUG-183/... into the manifest; caught before push by diffing a second regeneration, so I re-ran the ingest in the canonical checkout and the committed manifest names /home/kara/auger/docs/... Regeneration is therefore path-of-invocation dependent and will silently re-point a committed manifest when run from a worktree. Row stays in_progress because no GitReins verdict exists for aab0e5e, so no evidence_run_id is claimed (verdict debt).", "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": "aab0e5ea6b04ae70e637d61d3df4353c20c70331", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worktree": null, "branch": null, "sessions": null, "type": null, "worker_summary": "CI-red fix certified by judged verdict 6db67ef6: tier1 GATE PASS 797 passed / 2 skipped in 872.82s, live arms 2/0; tier2 PASS 5/5 with the evaluator re-running every proof.", "evidence_run_id": "6db67ef6"}
-{"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-184", "title": "[P2] acceptance-criteria repair: 14 of 27 open rows fail the deterministic dispatchability gate on unexpanded placeholders, so workers must invent paths and commands", "detail": {"metadata": {}, "fingerprint": "8eaafc9c1c7716fe4794c74fb38ed978ead003aaf8abfec4b0b9234f32c8679e"}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": "COS card manager measurement 2026-11-17T14:35Z on board @700ec56: `python3 ~/.hermes/scripts/acceptance_gate.py audit /home/kara/auger` reports 27 open rows, 14 failing, 13 passing. Every failure is the placeholder arm (angle-bracket stubs such as a bare token, namespace, key, run id, corpus path, verb name) with a few also failing the path arm where a criteria line names a path that is not in this repo's git ls-files (AUG-178's src/search/index.ts is duckbrain-owned) and one failing the outcome arm. The consequence is measurable: the open rows on this board are not re-runnable by a worker with no context, so each dispatch re-derives paths and commands from scratch, and the gate cannot be used as a dispatch filter. This is mechanical criteria maintenance — paths, commands and observables already exist in each row's own reasoning — not a redesign of any requirement, which is why it is filed as one chore rather than 14 edits by an out-of-lane writer. The COS does not rewrite foreman rows mid-flight (guardrail 2). Goal cards citing this work: t_a2ee1356 (QA trust) for the QA-plane rows, t_d7ac1156 (docs parity) for the DOC/doc-plane rows, t_35d10e68 (corpus/search) for the corpus rows.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "AC1 CENSUS ZERO: Run `python3 ~/.hermes/scripts/acceptance_gate.py audit /home/kara/auger | grep -c '^FAIL'`; expect the printed count to be 0 (measured 2026-11-17: 14). FAILIF: any FAIL line remains.\nAC2 SAME INTENT, RUNNABLE ARMS: Run `python3 ~/.hermes/scripts/acceptance_gate.py audit /home/kara/auger`; expect a PASS line for each of AUG-152, AUG-153, AUG-155, AUG-160, AUG-164, AUG-168, AUG-170, AUG-171, AUG-175, QA-AUGER-11-R4, REVIEW-AUGER-007, AUG-178, AUG-180, AUG-181 and AUG-182. FAILIF: any of those ids still prints FAIL, or a criterion was weakened into prose that names no command and no observable outcome.\nAC3 SCOPE OF THE EDIT: Run `git show --stat HEAD`; expect it to name .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl only. FAILIF: a source, test or docs file changes in the repair commit.\nAC4 INTENT PRESERVED: Run `git diff HEAD~1 -- .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl | grep -c '^-.*\"status\"'`; expect the printed count to be 0, so no row status, priority, commit_hash or evidence field moves during the rewrite. FAILIF: a status or evidence field is rewritten.\nAC5 NO SECRET IN CRITERIA: Run `git grep -nE '(sk-[A-Za-z0-9]{16,}|x-api-key: [A-Za-z0-9]{12,})' -- .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl`; expect exit code 1 with no matches, so a secret placeholder is replaced by a token-FILE read path such as /home/kara/.duckbrain/cos-sync.token and never by a literal key. FAILIF: any credential literal is introduced.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-17T14:37:02Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-17T14:37:02Z", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null, "sessions": null, "type": "chore"}
